DOLLY 7
PACKAGE airtime-godot
REQUIRES HOST runtime@0
REQUIRES HOST audio@0
REQUIRES HOST display@0
REQUIRES HOST input@0
REQUIRES HOST threads@0
REQUIRES HOST sockets@0
REQUIRES HOST gpu@0
REQUIRES HOST clipboard@0

# Airtime: Foundry in Godot: the strafe trials of demos/bhop with Airtime's own movement and course
# (bunny-hop and air-strafe over pads that drop, 33 pads in four sections), drawn by Godot's
# Forward+ renderer on gpu@0 as a foundry at night over a sea of molten metal. Its project
# (demos/godot/airtime) is imported and exported here by Godot's editor, and airtime-godot plays
# the pack with godot, which installs with it. The project installs too, for the editor.
FROM /v0.1.6/Dollyfile-system 33e5bcf65ef4a634da5dbf8e291a379148e7971aa0411fe1bdaa4e0332f24b94
INSTALL /v0.1.6/demos/godot/Dollyfile-godot baadc1405822d84085538468420f096d55c4d809a1a112c100ad6076f3a1b16c
USE /v0.1.6/demos/godot/Dollyfile-godot-editor 331ba631756d21a69ab3046a333fa1cb4cedff191eb5b9ade6cac1147d23b470

REQUIRES TOOL cp
REQUIRES TOOL godot-editor
REQUIRES TOOL mkdir
REQUIRES TOOL rm
REQUIRES TOOL tar

SOURCE /v0.1.6/dist/static/godot/airtime.tar e84cc87029526665f9e667809426f6d443771bb7e06833c62cc59f730423b260 /tmp/airtime.tar
SLOP CWD / tar -xf /tmp/airtime.tar
SLOP mkdir -p /usr/share/airtime-godot
SLOP cp -r /usr/src/airtime /usr/share/airtime-godot/project
SLOP CWD /usr/src/airtime godot-editor --headless --import
SLOP CWD /usr/src/airtime godot-editor --headless --export-pack Dolly /usr/share/airtime-godot/airtime.pck
SLOP rm -rf /usr/src/airtime /tmp/airtime.tar

FILE /usr/bin/airtime-godot
    #!/bin/slop
    godot --main-pack /usr/share/airtime-godot/airtime.pck "$@"
EXPORTS TOOL airtime-godot
FILE /usr/share/man/cat1/airtime-godot.1
    airtime-godot [GODOT-OPTION...] [-- --autopilot SECONDS]
    Plays Airtime: Foundry in Godot, the strafe trials of bhop with Airtime's own
    movement and course. A click takes the mouse; A and D with the mouse turning
    build speed in the air, Space or the wheel jumps, Escape gives the mouse back,
    R restarts, F returns to the last checkpoint, 1-4 practise a section, Q quits.
    Amber pads drop a moment after a landing; cyan decks hold. With --autopilot it
    plays a run by itself for that many seconds and prints how far it got. It
    draws through WebGPU (gpu@0). Its project is /usr/share/airtime-godot/project:
    copy it to edit it with godot-editor.
FILE /usr/share/airtime-godot/airtime.pck
FOLDER /usr/share/airtime-godot/project
